# Credentials — never commit. The pre-commit secret guard is the backstop;
# this entry is the primary control. See specs/ D2, D11, D14.
.env

# Publication-deferred material (build log, drafts, anything not yet decided).
# Named generically on purpose: a committed .gitignore listing specific
# filenames would itself disclose what is being withheld.
private/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Tooling caches
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
build/

# The findings review worksheet is rendered on demand, not committed (D76).
# Its purpose -- scaffolding for the one phase-1 step a model must not do -- was
# discharged when the last ruling landed, and it was never used for it:
# adjudication happened in dialogue and landed in corpus/findings.adjudication.yaml.
# What remained was 221KB of derived text whose own preamble had gone stale.
#     python tools/make_review_worksheet.py            # to the default path
#     python tools/make_review_worksheet.py --out X.md # anywhere
corpus/findings.review-worksheet.md

# The comparative-judgment store: the pairwise comparison log, built by
# `cj compare` and read by `cj fit`/`cuts`/`export`. Not committed — only its
# hash travels, in the severity file's `comparison_log_hash`, which is what
# makes severity provenance checkable without publishing every judgment.
# Recreate with `cj init --store .cj-store` and re-run the loop; the log is a
# record of one rater's session, not a project artifact.
.cj-store/

# Written by the session-resume tooling on this machine, in the repository root
# where `git add` would reach it. Absolute Windows paths and a session UUID — it
# describes one workstation, not the project.
resume_session.txt

# Judged run logs. Every judged run writes one, in both modes, so this
# directory fills up with per-run files that describe one invocation — except
# the reference log, which is the artifact replay mode exists to replay (D8)
# and is committed by name. `runs/*` rather than `runs/`, because a directory
# excluded wholesale cannot have a file re-included from inside it.
runs/*
!runs/reference-*.jsonl

# And one fossil, kept by name. `runs/measured/` holds a log recorded against a
# rubric this project has since changed, kept because the change **removed the
# measurement from the current log**: D132's precondition means the dimension
# produces no verdict for a call that retrieved no policy, so the verdicts D125
# and D132 both rest on are unreadable in anything recorded afterwards. Nothing
# replays it and nothing should; it is read.
!runs/measured/
!runs/measured/*.jsonl

# The report snapshot is NOT here, and `build/` is. The snapshot is the
# committed artifact the golden regression compares against (D8), so it lives
# in `snapshots/` where a mechanism reads it by name -- `build/` is where
# generated intermediates go, and a snapshot generated into a directory nobody
# commits is a regression test comparing a run against itself.

# The sibling repository, when it is checked out inside this root. CI does exactly
# that for the interface scanner (`path: comparative-judgment`), and a session may
# do it by hand. It is another repository's working copy, never this one's, and
# D207 has the license check skip a directory carrying its own `.git` for the same
# reason -- the ignore keeps `git status` honest, the check does not depend on it.
comparative-judgment/
